1. Explain why const constructors improve FPS during scrolling.

Ans :- Const constructors help improve FPS because Flutter does not rebuild widgets that are already constant.
When scrolling a long list, Flutter rebuilds many widgets repeatedly. If widgets are marked as const, Flutter 
reuses them instead of creating new objects again and again.
This reduces memory usage and rendering work, which makes scrolling smoother and improves application performance.

Ex:-
const Text("Hello")

Here Flutter knows the widget will never change, so it optimizes rendering.

2. Explain why InheritedWidget (or Provider) outperforms "lifting state up" for cross-tab data.

Ans :- When we lift state up, we pass data manually from parent to child widgets.
In large applications with many screens or tabs, this becomes difficult to manage.
InheritedWidget or Provider allows data sharing globally without passing it through every widget.

Advantages:
Cleaner code
Better performance
Easy state management
Less rebuilds
Easier maintenance

For cross-tab communication, Provider is more efficient because all tabs can access shared data directly.

3. Explain the difference between MainAxisAlignment and CrossAxisAlignment in a Row.

Ans :- In a Row widget:

MainAxisAlignment controls alignment horizontally because Row’s main axis is horizontal.
CrossAxisAlignment controls alignment vertically.

Ex:- 
Row(
  mainAxisAlignment: MainAxisAlignment.spaceEvenly,
  crossAxisAlignment: CrossAxisAlignment.center,
)

Here:
Widgets are spaced evenly horizontally
Widgets are centered vertically

4. Explain why a Stack widget is used for overlaying UI elements.

Ans :- A Stack widget is used when we want widgets to appear on top of each other.

It is useful for:-
Profile image with edit icon
Text over image
Notification badges
Floating buttons over UI

Ex:-
Stack(
  children: [
    Image.asset("image.png"),
    Positioned(
      bottom: 0,
      right: 0,
      child: Icon(Icons.edit),
    ),
  ],
)

5. Explain the role of ValueKey when reordering items in a list.

Ans :- ValueKey helps Flutter identify widgets uniquely during rebuilds or reordering.
Without keys, Flutter may confuse list items and update the wrong widget.

Using ValueKey:-
Preserves widget state
Improves performance
Maintains correct order

Ex:-
ListTile(
  key: ValueKey(item.id),
)
